<title>USA: Kansas feedlot cattle market roundup - USDA.</title>
<headline>Kansas feedlot cattle market roundup - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade was quiet, with no sales slaughter steers or heifers confirmed, USDA said. Inquiry and demand moderate. Sales confirmed on 1,900 cattle for the week to date including late Friday and the weekend, mostly previously contracted or formulated cattle.</p>
<p>The last established price was $66.00 on Friday. Asking</p>
<p>prices $67.00-$68.00, bids $65.00-$66.00 Monday.</p>
<p>Confirmed -   none   last week - none    last year - none</p>
<p>Wk to date - 1,900   last week - 1,000   last year - 900</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
